  "notes": "The 2012 Saudia passenger scheme (no longer the airline's newest) plus 'CARGO'. Measured on HZ-AK71 (right, 2024-05-12; mirrored into left-side coordinates) and HZ-AK74 (left, 2024-08-06): on both sides the SAUDIA block is forward and CARGO aft. The emblem's ring and the 777's raked tips plain. No photo yet shows a freighter in the 2023 green scheme; the four 777Fs ordered in 2026 (deliveries from late 2026) may arrive in it. The belly wasn't seen from below. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on HZ-AK71 (right, 2024-05-12) and HZ-AK74 (left, 2024-08-06): the name block (Arabic over SAUDIA) and CARGO read SAUDIA CARGO on both sides, so the name block is forward of CARGO on the left (x ~0.244) and aft of it on the right (~0.53, CARGO 0.341-0.52): each side now has its own set (the right had shown CARGO aft). Lengths measured: CARGO 0.18, SAUDIA 0.088, the Arabic 0.09.",
  "history": "New file. Saudia Cargo's freighters wear the 2012 scheme with 'CARGO' titles; the passenger fleet has moved to the 2023 green scheme (SVA/standard)."
